WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:09.680
The United States has an opportunity in
Libya. Resolving the Libya crisis is a

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:13.580
low-risk, high-reward option to weaken
Isis and al-Qaeda.

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:16.830
Libya's challenges are complex, but
fixable,

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:21.359
and solving them will have positive
effects on three continents. The U.S.

00:00:21.359 --> 00:00:25.199
tried to defeat Isis in Libya, and to
contain the regional impacts of the

00:00:25.199 --> 00:00:29.490
Libyan civil war. It failed. America backed Libyan partners

00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:34.110
that had one eye on fighting Isis and
the other on seizing territory. Conditions

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:38.010
that led to the rise of Isis in Libya
remain, and al-Qaeda is building a base

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:42.570
under the radar. Russia looks to use its
growing military and economic influence

00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:47.430
in Libya to undermine NATO in the
Mediterranean and pressure the EU. Libya

00:00:47.430 --> 00:00:52.060
could be the place for the U.S. to
strike a major blow against Isis and al-Qaeda.

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:55.739
A smart intervention to end the
civil war and rollback both groups is

00:00:55.739 --> 00:00:59.730
the best option. The U.S. should take
back leadership and coordinate its

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:04.140
allies and partners to shape a durable
outcome. The alternative is an unending

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:06.680
and expensive counterterrorism campaign.

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:12.280
What role should the U.S. take in Libya, if any? Let us know in your comments.

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:14.840
Also, let us know what other topics you'd like

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:18.920
our scholars to cover in 60 seconds, and
be sure to like and subscribe for more

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:22.970
research and videos from AEI.

